        "Manage risk by implementing systems to identify, assess, monitor, control standards and by reviewing performance. These are to be documented, maintained, audited and certification is to be retained wherever applicable.",
        "Provide appropriate IMS resources, like welfare facilities (including required information), well-maintained environment, procurement of energy efficient and safe work equipment, quality products and services, in order to facilitate effective IMS management to all stakeholders.",
        "Maintain communication, consultation, and participation of workers and other stakeholders to IMS including this policy and share the information with relevant government and non-government organizations as required and expected from entity with aim of development of legislations and standards.",
